#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Local stdio MCP server exposing the knowledge-tree workflow as tools.

Every operation is delegated to the sibling `kt` CLI, so revision conflicts, access
policy, locking, proof invalidation, and inode preservation stay owned by the CLI.
The one deliberate exception is access approval: `kt_access_request` asks the user
through the harness (MCP elicitation) and persists an accepted grant with the CLI's
own `apply_access_decision`. The model never sees or answers that prompt.
"""

